Strawberry 1.2.31

The official Ubuntu Noble amd64 package is obtained unchanged from:
https://github.com/strawberrymusicplayer/strawberry/releases/download/1.2.31/strawberry_1.2.31-noble_amd64.deb
SOURCE.json identifies the release files and their SHA-256 values. The executable
and package resources are unmodified. LICENSE contains the GPL version 3 text;
Strawberry is licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later. LICENSES/strawberry-package.txt
contains the original package component notices, which also remain in
runtime/usr/share/doc/strawberry/copyright after installation.

Complete corresponding source is retained as strawberry-1.2.31.tar.xz and is
available from:
https://github.com/strawberrymusicplayer/strawberry/releases/download/1.2.31/strawberry-1.2.31.tar.xz
https://github.com/strawberrymusicplayer/strawberry/tree/1.2.31
Build instructions are in that source release's README.md, CMakeLists.txt and
debian/ directory. schema.sql is an unchanged copy of data/schema/schema.sql.

The separate strawberry_start.py launcher initializes the normal configuration
and database with one empty playlist and the supplied music collection folder,
and disables the first-run sponsorship message. No upstream code is patched.

Copyright Strawberry developers and the contributors named in the upstream
source. This distribution is not affiliated with or endorsed by the project.

process_guard.c is a separate runtime boundary, compiled at installation. It
uses Linux Landlock to confine writes and child-process execution. It does not
modify upstream application files.
